a.expense\",\nevidence/native_run/observations/step_002.json:1452:      \"resource_name\": \"com.arduia.expense:id/tv_amount\",\nevidence/native_run/observations/step_002.json:1479:      \"package_name\": \"com.arduia.expense\",\nevidence/native_run/observations/step_002.json:1481:      \"resource_name\": \"com.arduia.expense:id/tv_currency_symbol\",\nevidence/native_run/openrouter_calls/call-0017.json:9:        \"content\": \"You are an agent who can operate an Android phone on behalf of a user. Based on user's goal/request, you may\\n- Answer back if the request/goal is a question (or a chat message), like user asks \\\"What is my schedule for today?\\\".\\n- Complete some tasks described in the requests/goals by performing actions (step by step) on the phone.\\n\\nWhen given a user request, you will try to complete it step by step. At each step, a list of descriptions for most UI elements on the current screen will be given to you (each element can be specified by an index), together with a history of what you have done in previous steps. Based on these pieces of information and the goal, you must choose to perform one of the action in the following list (action description followed by the JSON format) by outputing the action in the correct JSON format.\\n- If you think the task has been completed, finish the task by using the status action with complete as goal_status: `{\\\"action_type\\\": \\\"status\\\", \\\"goal_status\\\": \\\"complete\\\"}`\\n- If you think the task is not feasible (including cases like you don't have enough information or can not perform some necessary actions), finish by using the `status` action with infeasible as goal_status: `{\\\"action_type\\\": \\\"status\\\", \\\"goal_status\\\": \\\"infeasible\\\"}`\\n- Answer user's question: `{\\\"action_type\\\": \\\"answer\\\", \\\"text\\\": \\\"<answer_text>\\\"}`\\n- Click/tap on a UI element (specified by its index) on the screen: `{\\\"action_type\\\": \\\"click\\\", \\\"index\\\": <target_index>}`.\\n- Long press on a UI element (specified by its index) on the screen: `{\\\"action_type\\\": \\\"long_press\\\", \\\"index\\\": <target_index>}`.\\n- Type text into an editable text field (specified by its index), this action contains clicking the text field, typing in the text and pressing the enter, so no need to click on the target field to start: `{\\\"action_type\\\": \\\"input_text\\\", \\\"text\\\": <text_input>, \\\"index\\\": <target_index>}`\\n- Press the Enter key: `{\\\"action_type\\\": \\\"keyboard_enter\\\"}`\\n- Navigate to the home screen: `{\\\"action_type\\\": \\\"navigate_home\\\"}`\\n- Navigate back: `{\\\"action_type\\\": \\\"navigate_back\\\"}`\\n- Scroll the screen or a scrollable UI element in one of the four directions, use the same numeric index as above if you want to scroll a specific UI element, leave it empty when scroll the whole screen: `{\\\"action_type\\\": \\\"scroll\\\", \\\"direction\\\": <up, down, left, right>, \\\"index\\\": <optional_target_index>}`\\n- Open an app (nothing will happen if the app is not installed): `{\\\"action_type\\\": \\\"open_app\\\", \\\"app_name\\\": <name>}`\\n- Wait for the screen to update: `{\\\"action_type\\\": \\\"wait\\\"}`\\n\\nThe current user goal/request is: Add the following expenses into the pro expense:\\nname|amount_dollars|category_name|note\\nShirt Purchase|$446.34|Clothes|Want to have\\n\\nHere is a history of what you have done so far:\\nStep 1: Action selected: {\\\"action_type\\\": \\\"open_app\\\", \\\"app_name\\\": \\\"Pro Expense\\\"}. Opened the Pro Expense app from the home screen; app launched successfully (package changed to com.arduia.expense), ready to navigate to add a new expense entry for \\\"Shirt Purchase\\\" ($446.34, Clothes, \\\"Want to have\\\").\\nStep 2: Action selected: {\\\"action_type\\\": \\\"click\\\", \\\"index\\\": 0}. Clicked the floating \\\"+\\\" add button on the Pro Expense home screen, which successfully opened the Expense Entry form with fields for Name, Amount, Category (Food, Income, Housing, Social, Entertainment visible, may need to scroll for Clothes), Note, and a SAVE button. Next, fill in Name \\\"Shirt Purchase\\\", Amount \\\"446.34\\\", select Clothes category, and add note \\\"Want to have\\\".\\nStep 3: Action selected: {\\\"action_type\\\": \\\"input_text\\\", \\\"text\\\": \\\"Shirt Purchase\\\", \\\"index\\\": 6}. Entered \\\"Shirt Purchase\\\" into the Name field successfully; the Name field now shows \\\"Shirt Purchase\\\". Next, I need to input the amount (446.34) into the Amount field, select the Clothes category, and add the note \\\"Want to have\\\" before saving.\\nStep 4: Action selected: {\\\"action_type\\\": \\\"input_text\\\", \\\"text\\\": \\\"446.34\\\", \\\"index\\\": 7}. Entered \\\"446.34\\\" into the Amount field; it now displays 446.34 as expected. Next, I should select the \\\"Clothes\\\" category (likely need to scroll the category list since it's not visible), then fill the Note field with \\\"Want to have\\\", and finally tap SAVE.\\nStep 5: Action selected: {\\\"action_type\\\": \\\"scroll\\\", \\\"direction\\\": \\\"right\\\", \\\"index\\\": 8}. Scrolled the category list right to reveal more categories; now Social, Entertainment, Transportation, Clothes, Health Care are visible. Next step: tap \\\"Clothes\\\" to select the category, then enter the note \\\"Want to have\\\" and save.\\nStep 6: Action selected: {\\\"action_type\\\": \\\"click\\\", \\\"index\\\": 16}. Tapped on the \\\"Clothes\\\" category (index 16) to select it for the Shirt Purchase expense; screen appears unchanged in description but the category should now be selected. Next, I need to fill in the Note field with \\\"Want to have\\\" and then tap SAVE.\\nStep 7: Action selected: {\\\"action_type\\\": \\\"input_text\\\", \\\"text\\\": \\\"Want to have\\\", \\\"index\\\": 10}. Entered \\\"Want to have\\\" into the Note field successfully; the note now shows \\\"Want to have\\\". Next step is to tap SAVE to save the expense entry.\\nStep 8: Action selected: {\\\"action_type\\\": \\\"click\\\", \\\"index\\\": 10}. Tapped SAVE button to save the Shirt Purchase expense ($446.34, Clothes, \\\"Want to have\\\"); action succeeded as the screen returned to the Home page showing the newly added \\\"Shirt Purchase\\\" entry at the top of the Recent list. Task complete.\\n\\nHere is a list of descriptions for some UI elements on the current screen:\\nUI element 0: UIElement(text=None, content_description=None, class_name='android.widget.ImageButton', bbox=None, bbox_pixels=BoundingBox(x_min=891, x_max=1038, y_min=2106, y_max=2253), hint_text=None, is_checked=False, is_checkable=False, is_clickable=True, is_editable=False, is_enabled=True, is_focused=False, is_focusable=True, is_long_clickable=False, is_scrollable=False, is_selected=False, is_visible=True, package_name='com.arduia.expense', resource_name='com.arduia.expense:id/fb_main_add', tooltip=None, resource_id=None, metadata=None)\\nUI element 1: UIElement(text=None, content_description=None, class_name='android.widget.ImageButton', bbox=None, bbox_pixels=BoundingBox(x_min=0, x_max=147, y_min=128, y_max=275), hint_text=None, is_checked=False, is_checkable=False, is_clickable=True, is_editable=False, is_enabled=True, is_focused=False, is_focusable=True, is_long_clickable=False, is_scrollable=False, is_selected=False, is_visible=True, package_name='com.arduia.expense', resource_name=None, tooltip=None, resource_id=None, metadata=None)\\nUI element 2: UIElement(text='Home', content_description=None, class_name='android.widget.TextView', bbox=None, bbox_pixels=BoundingBox(x_min=189, x_max=334, y_min=166, y_max=237), hint_text=None, is_checked=False, is_checkable=False, is_clickable=False, is_editable=False, is_enabled=True, is_focused=False, is_focusable=False, is_long_clickable=False, is_scrollable=False, is_selected=False, is_visible=True, package_name='com.arduia.expense', resource_name=None, tooltip=None, res